LEVEL1:
Initial approval authority in the workflow.
Typically operational or department-level approver roles.

LEVEL2:
Second-level approval providing functional or managerial review.
Usually purchasing, finance, or line management roles.

LEVEL3:
Senior functional approval level.
Ensures compliance with financial, procurement, or governance rules.

LEVEL4:
Advanced or specialized approval authority.
Used for high-value, legal, HR, or risk-related reviews.

LEVEL5:
Senior management approval level.
Applied to critical or high-impact transactions.

LEVEL6:
Upper management or corporate approval authority.
Triggered for strategic or very high-value requests.

LEVEL7:
Executive-level approval authority.
Used only for exceptional or escalated cases.

LEVEL8:
Highest approval authority in the workflow.
Reserved for top executive or governance approvals.
